WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.370
Tom Sachs: Avoid camera movement.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.240
Film Courage: Especially with a DSLR like
a T2i?

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:13.299
Tom Sachs: Any camera, whether it’s a DSLR
or a red or any camera.

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:14.500
Camera movement is a privilege.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.690
It’s not a right.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:25.230
It’s an indulgence…you should do as little
work as you can…an idea shouldn’t be anymore…Einstein

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:30.140
said this….and [pauses to think] I’m going
to screw this up…everything should be as

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.360
simple as possible but no more so.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.460
In other words, use a tracking shot.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.270
Zoom in but only to an effect or a better
example may be omit unnecessary words [referring

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.230
to Authors Strunk and White].

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.680
A sculpture should be as small as it can be
to communicate the idea.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.530
That might mean in needs to be the size of
a building in some cases but it could fit

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.010
in the palm of your hand.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.250
Everything else is just hubris and ego.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.250
QUESTION FOR THE VIEWERS: Do you agree?

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:56.257
What are your thoughts on camera movement?

